cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this dataset, please cite it as below and link the study page."
type: dataset
title: "Hotel prices across booking sites: 17 snapshots, September 22 to October 10, 2026"
version: 1.0.0
date-released: "2026-10-10"
license: CC-BY-4.0
authors:
  - name: Underbook
    website: "https://underbook.co"
    email: hi@underbook.co
repository: "https://github.com/DPWonder/hotel-price-study"
url: "https://underbook.co/hotel-price-dispersion-study"
abstract: >-
  For each hotel, every booking site's nightly rate that Google Hotels listed for
  the same 2-night stay (2 adults, US market, US dollars), reduced to the going
  rate (the price most sites agree on), the cheapest price and the site that had
  it, whether that listing named a room, whether its room name matched the room
  at the going rate, whether fees were reported, and free cancellation. 17
  snapshots taken September 22 to October 10, 2026, with 7,044 priced hotel rows
  in 368 cities, plus two files that price the same stays again a week later.
  One CSV per snapshot, with a Frictionless datapackage.json.
keywords:
  - hotels
  - hotel prices
  - price dispersion
  - online travel agencies
  - booking sites
  - Google Hotels
  - travel
  - pricing
